                    <occupation>Publisher</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Se Ed Pope's note:Must be William Darton DNB 1755-1819 publisher and/or
                            his son William DNB 1781-1854. William senior had a son Thomas born
                            1783. Joseph Harvey 1764-1841 was a partner (see DNB for Darton). Like
                            Godwin they specialised in children's books. The 1810 entry suggests
                            that Godwin had a case against Darton in the Court of Requests, or he
                            went to watch someone else's case against Darton. I couldn't find it in
                            the newspapers, and Court of Requests records at Nat Arch cease in 1642.
                        </p>
